    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6-a11">

                <pb facs="0057" n="51" xml:id="pg51"/>

                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Captain Long</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Commanding U. S. S. Boston, Honolulu:</hi></p>
                <p>Where are you, chiefs, people and commons from my ancestor, and people from
                    foreign lands!</p>
                <p>Hear ye! I make known to you that I am in perplexity by reason of difficulties
                    into which I have been brought without cause; therefore, I have given away the
                    life of our land, hear ye! But my rule over you, my people, and your privileges
                    will continue, for I have hope that the life of the land will be restored when
                    my conduct is justified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Done at <placeName>Honolulu, Oahu</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1843-02-25">this twenty-fifth day of
                            February, 1843</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kamehameha III</hi></signed><lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Kekauluohi</hi></signed>.<lb/>Witness,<lb/><signed><hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">John D. Paalua.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>I hereby certify the above to be a faithful translation.</p>
                    <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. P. Judd</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Recorder and Translator for
                            Government</hi></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
